---
import PolicyPage from "../components/PolicyPage.astro";
import { pageSeo } from "../seo/registry.mjs";
---

<PolicyPage
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="Privacy Policy for 3Back, LLC."
	metadata={pageSeo["/privacy-policy"]}
>
	<h2>Privacy Policy for 3Back, LLC</h2>
	<p>Effective Date: September 6, 2026</p>
	<p>3Back, LLC (“we,” “our,” or “us”) Privacy Policy is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you visit our website <a href="https://3back.com">3back.com</a> (the “Site”) and outlines your privacy rights and how the law protects you.</p>
	<p>By using our Site, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy. If you do not agree with the terms of this Privacy Policy, please do not access the Site.</p>

	<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
	<p>We may collect and store the following types of information:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Personal Information:</strong> When you voluntarily provide it, such as when you register for our <a href="https://path.3back.com">courses</a>, subscribe to our newsletter, complete a contact form, or make a purchase. This may include your name, email address, mailing address, phone number, payment details, and other identifying information.</li>
		<li><strong>Automatically Collected Information:</strong> We may automatically collect certain information about your device and browsing habits when you access the Site. This includes your IP address, browser type, operating system, access times, and the pages you visit.</li>
		<li><strong>Cookies and similar technologies:</strong> We use cookies and similar technologies for site security and for measurement. The tools and purposes are described under Cookies and site measurement.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>2. Cookies and site measurement</h2>
	<p>3back.com uses a small set of measurement and security tools. We do not run advertising cookies or retargeting pixels on 3back.com. We do not sell personal information.</p>
	<p>Cloudflare provides hosting, security, and bot protection for the Site, including Turnstile on forms. Cloudflare Zaraz is the tag layer that loads the measurement tools below and records three outcome events: a conversation form succeeded, a No Head Works Alone paper request succeeded, and a Grip Check results submission succeeded. Those events do not include a name or email address in the event payload.</p>
	<p>Cloudflare Web Analytics provides aggregated visit counts. It is used to check that the site is being used. It is not used to build an advertising profile.</p>
	<p>Microsoft Clarity records how people move through pages. That can include session recordings and heatmaps. Clarity is used to see where the Site is confusing or broken. It is not used to serve ads.</p>
	<p>You can limit cookies in your browser. Microsoft also provides a Clarity opt-out at <a href="https://clarity.microsoft.com/opt-out">https://clarity.microsoft.com/opt-out</a>. Turning off cookies or using that opt-out can reduce how much measurement we receive. It does not delete information you already typed into a form.</p>
	<p>path.3back.com, event.3back.com, and other 3Back properties may use different processors and have their own notices.</p>

	<h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
	<p>We use the information we collect in the following ways:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>To provide and improve our services, including managing your course registrations and providing customer support.</li>
		<li>To personalize your experience on our Site and deliver content and product offerings relevant to your interests.</li>
		<li>To process your transactions, fulfill orders, and communicate with you regarding your purchases.</li>
		<li>To send you updates, newsletters, marketing materials, and other information that may be of interest to you. You can opt out of receiving these communications at any time.</li>
		<li>To monitor and analyze usage patterns on the Site and improve its functionality.</li>
		<li>To ensure security and prevent fraud.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>4. How We Share Your Information</h2>
	<p>We do not sell or rent your personal information to third parties. However, we may share your information in the following circumstances:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Service Providers:</strong> We may share your information with third-party service providers who assist us in operating our Site, conducting our business, and providing services to you. These providers are contractually bound to protect your information and may only use it for the purposes we specify.</li>
		<li><strong>Legal Requirements:</strong> We may disclose your information when required to comply with the law, enforce our Site policies, or protect our rights, property, or safety, or that of others.</li>
		<li><strong>Business Transfers:</strong> In the event of a merger, sale, or acquisition, your personal information may be transferred as part of the business assets.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>5. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
	<p>Depending on your location, you may have the following rights regarding your personal information:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Access:</strong> You may request access to the personal information we hold about you.</li>
		<li><strong>Correction:</strong> You may request that we correct any inaccuracies in your personal information.</li>
		<li><strong>Deletion:</strong> You may request that we delete your personal information, subject to certain legal obligations.</li>
		<li><strong>Opt-Out:</strong> You may opt out of marketing communications by following the instructions included in each email or by contacting us directly.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>To exercise these rights, please contact us at <a href="mailto:privacy@3back.com">privacy@3back.com</a>.</p>
	<p>Depending on your state, you may also have the right to know how we use personal information, to request a copy, to request deletion, and to appeal a refusal. We do not sell personal information or share it for cross-context behavioral advertising. To make a request, email privacy@3back.com.</p>

	<h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
	<p>We will retain your personal information for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes outlined in this Privacy Policy or as required by law. When personal information is no longer needed, we will securely delete or anonymize it.</p>

	<h2>7. Security of Your Information</h2>
	<p>We implement reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect your personal information from unauthorized access, disclosure, or misuse. However, no system is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee the absolute security of your data.</p>

	<h2>8. Third-Party Links</h2>
	<p>Our Site may contain links to third-party websites. We are not responsible for the privacy practices or content of these external sites. We encourage you to review the privacy policies of any third-party sites you visit.</p>

	<h2>9. Children’s Privacy</h2>
	<p>Our services are not directed to individuals under the age of 16. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 16. If you believe we have inadvertently collected such information, please contact us at <a href="mailto:privacy@3back.com">privacy@3back.com</a>, and we will take prompt action to delete it.</p>

	<h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
	<p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated effective date. We encourage you to review this policy periodically to stay informed about how we are protecting your information.</p>

	<h2>11. Contact Us</h2>
	<p>If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy or our data practices, please contact us at:</p>
	<p>3Back, LLC<br />Email: <a href="mailto:privacy@3back.com">privacy@3back.com</a></p>

	<hr />

	<p>This Privacy Policy was last updated on September 6, 2026.</p>
</PolicyPage>
